---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import GuideCard from '../components/GuideCard.astro';import {site,categories} from '../config';import {publishedArticles} from '../lib/content';
const posts=await publishedArticles();
---
<Base title={site.name} description="Clear Excel and Google Sheets guides, original practice data, and free browser tools. Fix formulas, clean CSVs, and get back to your work.">
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Practical help. One cell at a time.</p><h1 id="hero-title">Spreadsheet<br/>problems.<br/><em>Clearly solved.</em></h1><p>Make the formula work. Keep your data intact. Get a clear answer you can actually use.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/guides/">Find your next answer <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/tools/">Explore free tools →</a></div><div class="hero-note"><span class="checkmark">✓</span> Excel & Google Sheets <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> No account needed</div></div>
<div class="sheet-scene" aria-label="Illustrative sales worksheet. The two North Closed amounts total 600."><div class="sheet-decoration"></div><div class="sheet-window"><div class="sheet-toolbar"><span class="file-icon">▦</span> quarterly-sales.xlsx <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true">•••</span></div><div class="formula-bar"><span class="mono">E2 ▾</span><span class="mono">ƒx</span><code>=SUMIFS(C2:C5,A2:A5,"North",B2:B5,"Closed")</code></div><table class="mock-grid"><caption class="sr-only">Fictional sales data with a manually checked total</caption><thead><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="head"><td>1</td><td>Region</td><td>Status</td><td>Revenue</td></tr><tr class="matched"><td>2</td><td>North</td><td>Closed</td><td>240</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>South</td><td>Closed</td><td>180</td></tr><tr class="matched"><td>4</td><td>North</td><td>Closed</td><td>360</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>North</td><td>Open</td><td>90</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sheet-result"><span>North + Closed <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span><strong>600</strong><span>2 matching rows</span></div></div><div class="result-sticker"><span class="checkmark">✓</span><span><strong>Know why it works.</strong>Not just what to paste.</span></div></div></section>
<form class="search-band" action="/search/" role="search"><label for="home-search">What are you working on?</label><div class="search-form"><input id="home-search" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Try “leading zeros” or “XLOOKUP”"/><button type="submit">Find a guide ↗</button></div></form>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A good place to start</p><h2>A little less trial and error.</h2></div></div><div class="category-grid">{categories.map(c=><a class="category-tile" href={`/${c.slug}/`}><span class="category-icon" aria-hidden="true">{c.icon}</span><h3>{c.name}</h3><p>{c.description}</p></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="section section-rule"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Practical guides</p><h2>From stuck to sorted.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/">View all guides ↗</a></div><div class="guide-grid">{posts.slice(0,6).map((post,i)=><GuideCard post={post} number={i+1}/>)}</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="tool-feature"><div class="tool-feature-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Less busywork. More doing.</p><h2>Small tools. Real time saved.</h2></div><p>Free to use. Built for your browser.</p></div><div class="tool-promo"><span class="tool-promo-icon" aria-hidden="true">≋</span><div><h3>CSV Duplicate Checker</h3><p>Find matching rows, choose your key columns, and review what to keep before downloading.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/csv-duplicate-checker/">Check a CSV →</a></div></div><div class="tool-promo"><span class="tool-promo-icon" aria-hidden="true">ƒx</span><div><h3>Formula Finder</h3><p>A clear example for the job at hand. Explore eight everyday functions by task and app.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/formula-finder/">Find a formula →</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p><h2>Start with your problem.</h2></div></div><div class="problem-grid"><a class="problem-link" href="/troubleshooting/xlookup-not-working/"><span>“My lookup keeps returning an error.”</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="problem-link" href="/data-cleaning/import-csv-preserve-zeros-dates/"><span>“My IDs lost their leading zeros.”</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="problem-link" href="/data-cleaning/remove-duplicate-rows/"><span>“Which duplicate rows should I keep?”</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="problem-link" href="/formulas/sumifs-with-dates/"><span>“I need totals for a specific month.”</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="editorial-banner"><div><p class="eyebrow">Built on clear working</p><h2>Useful examples.<br/>Honest about the limits.</h2><p>We make the inputs, expected outputs, and sources visible—so you can follow the reasoning, not take our word for it.</p><a class="text-link" href="/editorial-policy/">How we check our guides ↗</a></div><div class="editorial-standards"><div><strong>Official sources first</strong><p>Microsoft and Google documentation, linked where it matters.</p></div><div><strong>Examples you can inspect</strong><p>Original, fictional datasets with explicit expected results.</p></div><div><strong>Clear testing boundaries</strong><p>A logical check is never presented as a live app test.</p></div><div><strong>An accountable publication</strong><p>Maintained by emfls, with <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">a real correction route</a>.</p></div></div></section>
</Base>
